From 35adca096eed563498dc90ccc8a52034afd8e7ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Crouse <mail@amz-x.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:21:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add Remote Desktop page using GNOME Remote Desktop

Lets the computer's screen be shared and optionally controlled over RDP
through gnome-remote-desktop. The page is only shown when
gnome-remote-desktop is installed.

Configuration goes through grdctl, which also enables and starts
gnome-remote-desktop.service and stores the login details in the keyring.
Turning it on first creates a self-signed TLS certificate with openssl,
stored where GNOME Settings keeps it, since the daemon refuses to serve RDP
without one. Login details are entered on the page and passed to grdctl on
stdin.

Based on the idea of #60 by DJABhipHop, ported to GTK4 and the current
SettingsPage layout.

Fixes #56

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
